    "narrative": "With the 2026 season nearing its conclusion, Ghost Ride the WHIP is operating under strict efficiency constraints to protect our game cap projections. Today\u2019s lone active entry is **Brice Turang**, who carries a marginal score of 47.02 against Rasmussen. While Rasmussen maintains a respectable 3.30 xERA, **Brice Turang** benefits from a dynamic platoon advantage against the right-hander and maintains high daily reliability. We are prioritizing his ability to manufacture stolen bases\u2014our most precious commodity\u2014over raw power output. His placement in the #5 spot provides sufficient RBI potential to justify the start, even if the matchup against a high-skill arm slightly suppresses his ceiling.\n\nThe remainder of our roster is idle, as our heavy hitters\u2014**Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood**\u2014are all facing team off-days. We are effectively in \"preservation mode\" to ensure that players like **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Mickey Moniak** remain available for higher-leverage matchups later in the week. The most difficult benching decision involved weighing the potential utility of **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Seiya Suzuki**, but with the current schedule, they fall into the \"Below floor\" category due to the lack of game availability. We continue to monitor the health status of **Tyler Soderstrom**, who remains on the IL; meanwhile, prospects like **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, and **Travis Bazzana** remain on our depth chart, biding their time until the rotation warrants their inclusion. With no inclement weather flags, the primary risk remains the stinginess of Rasmussen, but **Brice Turang**\u2019s speed profile remains our best bet for moving the needle in a stagnant Roto landscape.",
